  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Survivor Protection and Services</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cambodia is a source, transit, and destination country for men, women, and children trafficked into commercial sex work, domestic work, fishing, construction, agriculture, child sex tourism and begging. Consequently, the overall goal of this project is to strengthen survivor protection and services for all forms of trafficking in persons through: enhanced and consistent victim identification; demand driven delivery of services and reintegration options in provinces along Thailand-Cambodia border; and a series of trainings on victim identification and referral targeting law enforcement officials, border officials, prosecutors and community leaders.</narrative>
  </description>
